{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Dwell in the land which I shall tell you.</b> It makes no sense that He would say in a single breath: \"Dwell in the land which I shall tell you\" and \"Sojourn in this land.\" Rather, its meaning is: Do not go down to Egypt, but dwell all your days in the land that I tell you at every time — journey by the word of YHWH and encamp by the word of YHWH. And: \"Sojourn now in this land\" — in the land of the Philistines — \"for to you and to your seed I shall give it,\" as it is written (Joshua 13:3): \"the five lords of the Philistines are reckoned among the Canaanites.\" And it is possible that \"and He appeared to him\" is to be read as anterior, for before he departed from his place he was told: Do not go down to Egypt; dwell in the land which I shall tell you while you are there, and \"sojourn now in this land\" — in the land of Canaan, which encompasses many peoples and many lands, for I now command you never to depart from it, for all these lands I shall give to your seed. Now he departed from his place because of the famine, to journey throughout all the lands of Canaan and to dwell in the land that He would tell him, and when he came to Gerar, He said to him: Here you shall dwell. And there was no need to elaborate, for it is well known that he did not transgress the command of HaShem. And similarly: \"upon one of the mountains which I shall tell you\" (Genesis 22:2), as I have already mentioned (ibid. verse 9)."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:21:38.014452313Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}